│ handling of the first line of a docstring. The min() function      │
│ incorrectly calculates the indentation for the first line because  │
│ it includes the first line itself in the lines[1:] slice. This     │
│ results in an incorrect indentation value and subsequent errors.   │
│                                                                    │
│ The fix is to simply remove the [1:] slice when calculating the    │
│ indentation. This ensures that the first line is not considered    │
│ when determining the indentation level.                            │
│                                                                    │
│ Here's the patch:                                                  │
│                                                                    │
