│ Okay, let’s address this persistent issue. I’ve realized the core  │
│ problem is that trim_docstring incorrectly handles the first line  │
│ of a docstring, leading to a no content permitted error when using │
│ the default-role directive in Docutils. The fix is to skip the     │
│ first line when calculating the indentation.                       │
│                                                                    │
│ Here’s the reasoning:                                              │
│                                                                    │
│ The trim_docstring function calculates the indentation of each     │
│ line in the docstring. The issue arises because the first line,    │
│ which often doesn't have any leading whitespace, results in an     │
│ indentation of 0. Docutils expects non-empty first lines to have a │
│ non-zero indentation. By skipping the first line, we ensure that   │
│ the indentation calculation is correct for subsequent lines.       │
│                                                                    │
│ Here's the patch:                                                  │
│                                                                    │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
